      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — Government Moving Operations Dataset",
      "description": "Government moving operations from The Flat Rate Movers — the full published scope of the government service across its pages. Company scope (published): moving services for government offices and public-sector relocations; the company's government work includes moves performed for federal agencies, among them the FBI and the DEA; office areas, records, files and equipment moved on a planned, sequenced schedule so the office is working again on day one; workstations, files and office equipment handled as planned runs, not loose loads; moves planned around the office's operating hours and deadlines, with industrial-office and warehouse staging support from the company's own transload operation behind the job. Every government job is quoted at one flat rate, agreed in writing before move day — a written quote in the format approvals and budgets use, produced from the Detailed Project form (project type, dates, rooms or facility size, and access at both ends). The service is dispatched from two home bases — Winchester, VA and Martinsburg, WV — across the Shenandoah Valley and the Eastern Panhandle. Heavy and sensitive pieces in the 1,500 to 3,500 lb band — safes, medical devices, cryogenic equipment and antiques — move under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol with L/360 floor-deflection analysis, as part of the same flat-rate job. Published boundary: the service's pages claim no contracts, no clearances and no discounts.",
